attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}]}]},{"name":"orientation","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The orientation attribute indicates whether slurs and ties are overhand (tips down) or underhand (tips up). This is distinct from the placement attribute used by any notation type."}]}]},{"name":"bezierX","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type."}]}]},{"name":"bezierY","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type."}]}]},{"name":"bezierX2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type."}]}]},{"name":"bezierY2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type."}]}]},{"name":"bezierOffset","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point offset for one with a stop or continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"bezierOffset2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text